Digin is proprietary software. It is not open source, and nothing in this
repository is offered under an open source license. This file says what you
may do with Digin without a signed agreement. Where arlint.dev has signed a
license agreement with you, that agreement governs instead.

"Digin" means the Digin software, including the container images published
at ghcr.io/arlintdev/digin and the server and web application in them.
"Install files" means the Helm chart, the Docker Compose files and the other
files in this repository.

1. EVALUATION

   Anyone may install and run Digin to evaluate it, for 90 days from the day
   the installation first starts. During those 90 days you may:

   a. pull the images from ghcr.io/arlintdev/digin and run them on systems
      you control, or that are controlled for you;
   b. let the people evaluating Digin with you use it;
   c. keep copies of the images inside your own environment, such as a
      private registry, only as needed to run the evaluation.

   An evaluation is not production. You may not use Digin during an
   evaluation to run your business or mission, to hold records you rely on,
   or to serve people who are not evaluating it.

2. AFTER 90 DAYS

   After 90 days, continuing to run Digin requires a written license from
   arlint.dev and the license key it issues. Without one, Digin becomes
   read-only: people can sign in, read and export what is there, and nothing
   can be created or changed. Starting a new installation to begin another
   evaluation period is not permitted without written permission.

   To buy a license: sales@digin.work.

3. WHAT IS NOT GRANTED

   Unless arlint.dev agrees in writing, you may not:

   a. redistribute, publish, sell, rent or sublicense the images or any part
      of Digin, or make them available to anyone outside your organization;
   b. offer Digin, or anything built from it, to others as a hosted service;
   c. copy, modify, decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer Digin, or
      remove, disable or work around its license check, except where the
      law allows this despite this restriction;
   d. use Digin to build a competing product.

   You get no right to Digin's source code. All rights not expressly granted
   here are reserved by arlint.dev.

4. THE INSTALL FILES

   You may copy, modify and use the install files for the purpose of
   installing and running Digin under this license or a signed agreement,
   and share them, modified or not, with others who will run Digin under the
   same terms. They grant no rights to Digin itself.

5. THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE

   The images include third-party software under its own licenses, listed in
   the bills of materials in the image at /usr/share/digin/sbom/. The install
   files can also run software that is not Digin, such as PostgreSQL and
   ClamAV, under its own licenses. Those licenses govern that software, and
   nothing here narrows them.

6. ENDING

   This license ends at once if you break its terms. When it ends, or when
   the evaluation period is over without a written license, stop running
   Digin and delete the images, except for what you need to export your own
   data.

